    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud held talks with Dr. Mohammed bin Abdulkarim Al-Issa on strengthening Somalia's ties with the Muslim World League, focusing on religious affairs, peace, and social coexistence.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud met with Dr. Mohammed bin Abdulkarim Al-Issa, Secretary General of the Muslim World League and Chairman of the Council of Muslim Scholars, in Mogadishu on September 11, 2026. The meeting took place at the National Palace and centered on enhancing cooperation between Somalia and the Muslim World League, particularly in religious matters, peacebuilding, and fostering harmonious coexistence within communities.\n\nThe discussions also underscored the importance of continued collaboration to address shared challenges facing the Islamic world. Dr. Al-Issa's visit is part of the Muslim World League's broader engagement with member states and Muslim communities globally. The organization, based in Mecca, frequently facilitates interfaith dialogue and promotes moderate Islamic teachings.\n\nSomalia has maintained a relationship with the Muslim World League for years, with the League supporting various humanitarian and educational initiatives in the country. This latest meeting follows previous interactions between Somali officials and League representatives, signaling ongoing diplomatic engagement. President Hassan Sheikh, who assumed office in 2022, has prioritized international partnerships to support Somalia's stability and development.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the strengthening of ties with the Muslim World League could translate into increased support for religious institutions, educational programs, and community projects both in Somalia and abroad. Many diaspora Somalis maintain strong religious connections and often look to such partnerships for guidance and resources that benefit their communities.\n\nThe meeting reflects Somalia's continued efforts to engage with international Islamic bodies, which can enhance its standing in the Muslim world and attract further cooperation. No specific agreements or outcomes were disclosed, but both parties reaffirmed their commitment to working together on issues of mutual interest.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/09/12/xasan-sheekh-iyo-al-issa-oo-arrimo-xasaasi-ah-ka-wada-hadlay/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=xasan-sheekh-iyo-al-issa-oo-arrimo-xasaasi-ah-ka-wada-hadlay",
