    "summary": "Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre held an accountability and evaluation session with his cabinet, assessing progress against signed performance agreements and pledging adjustments where challenges arose.",
    "content": "Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre convened a meeting with federal cabinet ministers to review their performance over the past year. The session focused on measuring each minister's work against the commitments outlined in individual performance agreements signed at the start of their tenure.\n\nThe Prime Minister stated that the purpose of the review was to ensure accountability and to identify areas where targets were not met. He noted that where obstacles prevented the completion of certain tasks, the goals and timelines in the agreements would be revised accordingly.\n\nThis marks the first time the current government has conducted such a formal evaluation of its ministers. The move comes as the administration faces mounting pressure to deliver on promises related to security, economic reform, and public service delivery.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, which closely follows developments in Mogadishu and often contributes to reconstruction and development efforts, the review signals a push for greater transparency and results from the federal government. Many diaspora members have invested in or supported projects tied to government ministries, and they stand to benefit from improved accountability.\n\nThe Prime Minister's office did not specify which ministries were found lacking or what specific adjustments would be made. Further details on the evaluation outcomes are expected in the coming weeks.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/12/%f0%9d%90%91%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%a2%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%ae%f0%9d%90%a5-%f0%9d%90%96%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ac%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%9a%f0%9d%90%ab%f0%9d%90%9e-%f0%9d%90%97-2/",
